  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 104 PM MDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nMain impact today is significant smoke has moved into southeast\nIdaho and dropped daytime temperatures substantially from the\nprevious few days. Expected to get at least a bit of clearing\nTuesday but still lack confidence in widespread 90s in low\nelevations for high temperatures tomorrow. Air quality alerts\nhave been issued for a large portion of southeast Idaho for the\nsmoke present. Isolated showers and thunderstorms are expected\nthis evening as well as Tuesday and Wednesday in southwest flow\naloft. By Thursday upper level ridge begins to expand north and\ndry conditions are in the forecast grids Thursday through next\nMonday. With this extreme heat is expected to return with low\nelevation highs nearing 100 again both Friday and Saturday.\nPresence or non presence of smoke will be a factor in\ntemperatures for several days.",
